{
  "case_id": "2016-15-649",
  "document_hash": "36d580a49e0224a0cc5d59f1120e305f32eb5015b098dadd47100faaab4bc370",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2016-15-649",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "36d580a49e0224a0cc5d59f1120e305f32eb5015b098dadd47100faaab4bc370",
      "evidence_id": "ev-36d580a49e02-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What we had asked for before, and what may well make the most sense, is conversion to Chapter 7, in which case either the Chapter 7 trustee could pursue the fraudulent-transfer claim --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondents",
      "case_id": "2016-15-649",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "36d580a49e0224a0cc5d59f1120e305f32eb5015b098dadd47100faaab4bc370",
      "evidence_id": "ev-36d580a49e02-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "that a -- a court could not resolve a case by ordering the distribution of assets that would violate their priority scheme."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Harrington",
      "case_id": "2016-15-649",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "36d580a49e0224a0cc5d59f1120e305f32eb5015b098dadd47100faaab4bc370",
      "evidence_id": "ev-36d580a49e02-0001-0001",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "State assets don't belong to the debtor, and they don't belong to a subset of creditors. They belong to the estate."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2016-15-649",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "36d580a49e0224a0cc5d59f1120e305f32eb5015b098dadd47100faaab4bc370",
      "evidence_id": "ev-36d580a49e02-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What is your response to the argument that your argument regarding Section 103(a) makes the provisions that specifically make the priorities applicable in Chapter 7 and Chapter 11 superfluous?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2016-15-649",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "36d580a49e0224a0cc5d59f1120e305f32eb5015b098dadd47100faaab4bc370",
      "evidence_id": "ev-36d580a49e02-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 34,
        "start": 34
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "when you're in Chapter 11, doesn't the judge, the bankruptcy judge, have to approve that settlement?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2016-15-649",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "36d580a49e0224a0cc5d59f1120e305f32eb5015b098dadd47100faaab4bc370",
      "evidence_id": "ev-36d580a49e02-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: But -- but this seems -- but the essence of the case is not really an objection to approval of the settlement; it's the objection of the distribution of the assets."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. LANDAU",
      "case_id": "2016-15-649",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "36d580a49e0224a0cc5d59f1120e305f32eb5015b098dadd47100faaab4bc370",
      "evidence_id": "ev-36d580a49e02-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. LANDAU: Absolutely. And that's -- I think that's so critical, Your Honor, and -- and their objection would actually completely come back to bite them because there is no legal difference between a distribution of assets on the first day where they recovered $6 million in this case in their prepetition wage and benefit claims."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2016-15-649",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "36d580a49e0224a0cc5d59f1120e305f32eb5015b098dadd47100faaab4bc370",
      "evidence_id": "ev-36d580a49e02-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: But that's -- I see that point, which you've made several times, is a very good point. I -- clarify a basic misunderstanding on my part. What's a structured settlement?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. LANDAU",
      "case_id": "2016-15-649",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "36d580a49e0224a0cc5d59f1120e305f32eb5015b098dadd47100faaab4bc370",
      "evidence_id": "ev-36d580a49e02-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. LANDAU: Your Honor, I think what you are saying or the -- the point that you're getting to can be resolved through the traditional 363(b) analysis, which allows for play in the joints, unlike their unyielding and absolute -- absolute priority rule."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2016-15-649",
      "confidence": 0.8,
      "document_hash": "36d580a49e0224a0cc5d59f1120e305f32eb5015b098dadd47100faaab4bc370",
      "evidence_id": "ev-36d580a49e02-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: The question is whether Congress did enact it and what you can point to in the Bankruptcy Code that suggests that the continual statement that it's just one, two, three, four, five is subject to a kind of equitable exception for Pareto-superior outcomes."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2016-15-649",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "36d580a49e0224a0cc5d59f1120e305f32eb5015b098dadd47100faaab4bc370",
      "evidence_id": "ev-36d580a49e02-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: So how do you protect the excluded creditor from being preyed on by one of the other creditors? We already know the junior creditors have a self-interest."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. LANDAU",
      "case_id": "2016-15-649",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "36d580a49e0224a0cc5d59f1120e305f32eb5015b098dadd47100faaab4bc370",
      "evidence_id": "ev-36d580a49e02-0002-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 51,
        "start": 51
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. LANDAU: -- does the absolute priority rule apply to distributions of plan assets -- of -- of estate assets, excuse me -- before a plan? They say yes, it does. We say no, it doesn't."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2016-15-649",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "36d580a49e0224a0cc5d59f1120e305f32eb5015b098dadd47100faaab4bc370",
      "evidence_id": "ev-36d580a49e02-0002-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 52,
        "start": 52
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: But that's, I think, where the -- the -- the issue comes down. I mean, the reasonableness of your position is directly related to how extraordinary the extraordinary circumstances have to be."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Sun Life",
      "case_id": "2016-15-649",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "36d580a49e0224a0cc5d59f1120e305f32eb5015b098dadd47100faaab4bc370",
      "evidence_id": "ev-36d580a49e02-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. LANDAU: In the absence of a global settlement of this WARN claim outside of the -- against Sun, Sun didn't want to have a settlement that -- that funded the litigation against it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2016-15-649",
      "confidence": 0.93,
      "document_hash": "36d580a49e0224a0cc5d59f1120e305f32eb5015b098dadd47100faaab4bc370",
      "evidence_id": "ev-36d580a49e02-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Why did it care to exclude these truck drivers from receiving whatever they demanded?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2016-15-649",
      "confidence": 0.92,
      "document_hash": "36d580a49e0224a0cc5d59f1120e305f32eb5015b098dadd47100faaab4bc370",
      "evidence_id": "ev-36d580a49e02-0003-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 61,
        "start": 61
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: What the Code in 363(b) says is the trustee can sell a suit. Okay? That's what it says. It says nothing about --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2016-15-649",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "36d580a49e0224a0cc5d59f1120e305f32eb5015b098dadd47100faaab4bc370",
      "evidence_id": "ev-36d580a49e02-0003-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 63,
        "start": 63
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. SPINELLI: Respondents' position fails because Section 363(b) is not a means of distributing estate assets. The -- the 363(b) discretion that Mr. Landau referred to is discretion to approve a settlement or a sale of an estate asset, not to distribute the settlement or sale proceeds in violation of priority."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2016-15-649",
      "confidence": 0.0,
